      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "Why there are two // Slash for the division"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Nisha Sharma from Programiz"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Hello there, nice question!"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The double slash // is used in Python for integer division. Unlike the single slash /, which returns a decimal value, // divides the numbers and gives the result as a whole number. Since the formula for the sum of natural numbers always results in an integer, using // helps keep the output clean and avoids unnecessary decimal points."
    },
